        'What did change was the actress. Rhea Seehorn won for “Pluribus”, the science-fiction series Vince Gilligan wrote with her in mind after “Better Call Saul”, and she did it over Carrie Coon, Keri Russell, Chase Infiniti (“The Testaments”) and Zendaya, nominated for “Euphoria”. It confirms a career the industry took far too long to notice: Seehorn played six seasons of Kim Wexler without a single Emmy. Gilligan took writing for the episode “We Is Us”; directing went to Saul Metzstein for “Scars”, from “Slow Horses”. In supporting, Allison Janney for “The Diplomat” and Tom Pelphrey for “Task”, who dedicated his award to his fiancée Kaley Cuoco, “very pregnant” in the stalls, in the most cheered speech of the night.',
