        'Pattinson is Antinous, the ringleader of the suitors besieging Penelope in the palace of Ithaca while Odysseus fails to return. He has said he built him out of James Woods\'s Lester Diamond in “Casino”: a slimy man who knows he is not wanted and will not leave. He was, reportedly, the only cast member who asked to read the script before signing, which with Nolan almost nobody does. That a Homeric suitor is among the most talked-about characters of a three-hour film with a cyclops in it says a lot about what Pattinson does with a supporting part: he steals it from the leads without ever seeming to try.',
